    "question": {
      ":question/id": "bfb1e6e6-4429-5216-9520-da272758a196",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=- x^{3} - x$ at $\\left(-1,2\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- x^{3} - x$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=- 3 x^{2} - 1\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(-1\\right)=- 3 \\left(-1\\right)^{2} - 1=-4\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-4\\right)}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(2\\right)&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(-1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{4}+\\left(\\frac{1}{4}\\right)+\\left(2\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{4} + \\frac{9}{4}\\\\\n\\left(-4\\right)y&=-x+\\left(-1\\right)+\\left(-8\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(-4\\right)y&=-9\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $-4$ and the constant is $-9$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "94ca41df-1ca7-5fec-86ba-4fbff12229d9",
