    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fd2ff74c-a006-5ba9-ad6e-e47d1c6cb6fd",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=- 2 x^{2} - x - 1$ at $\\left(1,-4\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- 2 x^{2} - x - 1$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=- 4 x - 1\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(1\\right)=- 4 \\left(1\\right) - 1=-5\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-5\\right)}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-4\\right)&=\\frac{1}{5}\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5} - \\frac{21}{5}\\\\\n\\left(-5\\right)y&=-x+\\left(1\\right)+\\left(20\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(-5\\right)y&=21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $-5$ and the constant is $21$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0461f451-1384-59af-9544-88c4a5295b9d",
          ":answer-field/key": "coefficient",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
