    "question": {
      ":question/id": "10a875be-e0c2-510d-ac63-8e61d4802e96",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=x^{3} - x - 1$ at $\\left(2,5\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=x^{3} - x - 1$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3 x^{2} - 1\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=3 \\left(2\\right)^{2} - 1=11\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(11\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{11}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(5\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{11}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{11}+\\left(\\frac{2}{11}\\right)+\\left(5\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{57}{11} - \\frac{x}{11}\\\\\n\\left(11\\right)y&=-x+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(55\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(11\\right)y&=57\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $11$ and the constant is $57$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
