    "question": {
      ":question/id": "cb09b447-ff85-5e0a-a376-d65b44d36159",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=- x^{3} - 2 x$ at $\\left(1,-3\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- x^{3} - 2 x$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=- 3 x^{2} - 2\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(1\\right)=- 3 \\left(1\\right)^{2} - 2=-5\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-5\\right)}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-3\\right)&=\\frac{1}{5}\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)+\\left(-3\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5} - \\frac{16}{5}\\\\\n\\left(-5\\right)y&=-x+\\left(1\\right)+\\left(15\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(-5\\right)y&=16\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $-5$ and the constant is $16$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "46676dfd-44a2-5470-b72f-3223d140ebf1",
