    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d9b899ee-b6a1-53fb-be36-62a523372d69",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=x^{3} + x + 1$ at $\\left(-1,-1\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=x^{3} + x + 1$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3 x^{2} + 1\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(-1\\right)=3 \\left(-1\\right)^{2} + 1=4\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(4\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-1\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(-1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)+\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{4} - \\frac{5}{4}\\\\\n\\left(4\\right)y&=-x+\\left(-1\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(4\\right)y&=-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $4$ and the constant is $-5$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "954b1c31-490c-5bc1-9484-1595d3785964",
