    "question": {
      ":question/id": "be7a93b9-64d4-5e4a-af06-b10b4c0b581a",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=- x^{3} - 2 x - 2$ at $\\left(1,-5\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- x^{3} - 2 x - 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=- 3 x^{2} - 2\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(1\\right)=- 3 \\left(1\\right)^{2} - 2=-5\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(-5\\right)}=\\frac{1}{5}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-5\\right)&=\\frac{1}{5}\\left(x-\\left(1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{5}\\right)+\\left(-5\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{x}{5} - \\frac{26}{5}\\\\\n\\left(-5\\right)y&=-x+\\left(1\\right)+\\left(25\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(-5\\right)y&=26\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $-5$ and the constant is $26$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
