    "question": {
      ":question/id": "56a4b02d-b5ef-5af1-8e9a-eff9390c8216",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=- x^{2} + 2 x + 2$ at $\\left(-1,-1\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=- x^{2} + 2 x + 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=2 - 2 x\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(-1\\right)=2 - 2 \\left(-1\\right)=4\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(4\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-1\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{4}\\left(x-\\left(-1\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)+\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{4} - \\frac{5}{4}\\\\\n\\left(4\\right)y&=-x+\\left(-1\\right)+\\left(-4\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(4\\right)y&=-5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $4$ and the constant is $-5$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "03ab8459-8e4e-5e53-b3e4-8f8ca01ec5ab",
