    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a037dc83-8fc5-534e-99fc-defe818961ef",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{x^{6}}{8} - x^{3} - 1$ at $\\left(2,-1\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=\\frac{x^{6}}{8} - x^{3} - 1$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=\\frac{3 x^{5}}{4} - 3 x^{2}\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=\\frac{3 \\left(2\\right)^{5}}{4} - 3 \\left(2\\right)^{2}=12\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(12\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{12}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(-1\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{12}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{12}+\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)+\\left(-1\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{12} - \\frac{5}{6}\\\\\n\\left(12\\right)y&=-x+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(-12\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(12\\right)y&=-10\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $12$ and the constant is $-10$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
