    "question": {
      ":question/id": "d9c9ebe2-f350-57ea-81ba-f66ca1315833",
      ":question/problem": "Find the equation of the normal line to the curve $y=x^{3} + 2 x - 2$ at $\\left(2,10\\right)$.\n\nGive exact values of $a$ and $b$ in $x+ay=b$.\n\n$a=$ {{coefficient}}\n\n$b=$ {{constant}}",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Let $f(x)=x^{3} + 2 x - 2$. Differentiate:\n\n$$\nf'(x)=3 x^{2} + 2\n$$\n\nEvaluate the tangent slope at the supplied abscissa:\n\n$$\nm_t=f'\\left(2\\right)=3 \\left(2\\right)^{2} + 2=14\n$$\n\nThe normal is perpendicular to the tangent, so\n\n$$\nm_n=-\\frac{1}{m_t}=-\\frac{1}{\\left(14\\right)}=- \\frac{1}{14}.\n$$\n\nUse the point in point-slope form and rearrange:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny-\\left(10\\right)&=- \\frac{1}{14}\\left(x-\\left(2\\right)\\right)\\\\\ny&=- \\frac{x}{14}+\\left(\\frac{1}{7}\\right)+\\left(10\\right)\\\\\ny&=\\frac{71}{7} - \\frac{x}{14}\\\\\n\\left(14\\right)y&=-x+\\left(2\\right)+\\left(140\\right)\\\\\nx+\\left(14\\right)y&=142\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe coefficient is $14$ and the constant is $142$.",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
